ction, closure or accessor, a kind that isn’t a 32-bit literal other than 0, and a unique key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that is empty or sits in a private or fileprivate type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A member’s record names it through the enclosing types, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Scheduler.Jobs.clean","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which works","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in a class or an actor too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before swift-syntax 600 a macro can’t see its lexical context. There a type it registers must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be declared at file scope, a member’s record names it through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":", so a static member of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"class or an actor fails to compile in the expansion, and the compiler, not the macro, refuses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a local declaration or a member of a generic type, with an error in the expansion."}]}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetMacro","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetMacro","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"LinkerSetMacro","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}],"externalID":"s:22LinkerSetsMacroSupport0a3SetC0P","roleHeading":"Protocol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/LinkerSets\/blob\/main\/Sources\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro.swift#L55","fileName":"LinkerSetMacro.swift"}},"abstract":[{"text":"A macro that turns the declaration i